## 3. Track 2 — Submission

### Git Branch Workflow

Each final submission gets its own branch:

```
main                          ← development, experiments
├── submit/act-v1             ← first submission (frozen)
├── submit/act-v2             ← second submission (frozen)
└── submit/hybrid-v1          ← third submission (frozen)
```

Workflow:
```bash
# When ready to submit:
git checkout -b submit/act-v1
# Update Dockerfile CMD to point to the right policy
# Commit everything
git push origin submit/act-v1

# Build & push Docker image
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yaml build model
docker tag my-solution:v1 <ecr-uri>:act-v1
docker push <ecr-uri>:act-v1
```

### Submission Script

#### [NEW] [scripts/submit.sh](file:///home/user/aic/scripts/submit.sh)

```bash
./scripts/submit.sh act_baseline act-v1 "Baseline RunACT submission"
#                    ^ policy      ^ tag   ^ description
```

This script will:
1. **Create** git branch `submit/<tag>`
2. **Update** `docker/my_policy/Dockerfile` CMD to point to `aic_model.policies.<policy>`
3. **Commit** all changes
4. **Build** via `docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yaml build model`
5. **Run local verify** via `docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yaml up`
6. **Parse** results and append to `submission_log.yaml`
7. **Print** instructions for the ECR push (tag + push commands)
8. **Switch** back to `main` branch

